\[AB^2 = OA^2 + OB^2 - 2 \cdot OA \cdot OB \cdot \cos \angle AOB.\]Substituting $AB = 6$, $OA = OB = 6$, we get
\[36 = 36 + 36 - 72 \cos \angle AOB.\]Then $\cos \angle AOB = \frac{36}{72} = \frac{1}{2}$, so $\angle AOB = 60^\circ$.

